cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this testbed, cite the software. The corpus it generates is
  reproducible from a seed, so citing a version is citing the data.
title: "Pharos: a labeled corpus generator and acceptance gate for measuring a governed disclosure boundary"
abstract: >-
  Pharos generates a labeled corpus of maritime watch reporting whose objects
  carry classification levels and cross-cutting compartments over a product
  lattice, and gates whether a generated corpus may be used at all. It is the
  testbed a disclosure-boundary argument is measured on: the corpus, the
  acceptance gate that can refuse it, the simulated analyst fleet, and the
  aggregator-side machinery those measurements run through.
type: software
authors:
